{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership","id":1346711,"title":"Pack Membership","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-07T06:21:47-08:00","id":1346711,"title":"Pack Membership","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Do members of the pack, for purposes of Backgrounds, Gifts, Merits and Flaws; must be Werewolves only? Does the totem count? Does Kinfolk? Can you make a human part of it? A supernatural creature?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> <br /> (I was thinking for a mixed game, using the <i>Pack Mentality</i> flaw, but no one else seems to be going to use a Werewolf)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:55:47-08:00","id":1346757,"title":"","content":"For the default Garou Rite for forming a pack, all the members must be werewolves (the Totem isn't explicitly excluded, but I'd say the majority of the implicit phrasing leads to not including them).<br /> <br /> The multi-Changing Breed alliances (the Hengeyokai and Ahadi) have ways to include any Fera as part of a pack-equivalent.<br /> <br /> Be default anything else is excluded unless they can get access to a power that would allow them to on some level, plus some ST flexibility in most cases.<br /> <br /> A Kinfolk that learns the Tagalong Gift (which means being a Gnawer kin or at least being on super good terms with a Gnawer Theurge) can temporarily join packs.<br /> <br /> In general none of the Fera are accepting of other supernaturals in their packs/equivalents. It's possible with the right powers to make a cause some of them could join in the bond, but that doesn't mean they'd be allowed to (or that pack/etc. would be seen as traitors for doing it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T17:18:29-08:00","id":1346901,"title":"","content":"Wave Sentai aren't &quot;REal&quot; packs but might include nonFera outsiders. A couple of Totems say they will allow Kin in their packs.. that's pretty much it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:57:59-08:00","id":1347055,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1346901#post1346901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wave Sentai aren't &quot;REal&quot; packs but might include nonFera outsiders. A couple of Totems say they will allow Kin in their packs.. that's pretty much it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this the W20 Changing Breed book?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T15:45:16-08:00","id":1347116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347055#post1347055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is this the W20 Changing Breed book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Members<br /> of wave sentai can come from different courts and, on<br /> rare occasions, include Kumo or even shen from outside<br /> the Beast Courts. \u201cMountain\u201d sentai, on the other hand,<br /> are as enduring as their name. Established more for bonds<br /> of pack and family than to accomplish a specific task,<br /> members of mountain sentai always come from the same<br /> court, and share a single totem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cb 20<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated to this there are a few totems that in their write up mention allowing Kin as members Soldaris(sp) I think is one. Those you'd have to look up each spirit on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T03:38:59-08:00","id":1347436,"title":"","content":"Wave Sentai is nothing, but a bunch of (INSERT HERE) assembled to finish a task. They are not bound spiritualy, and not counts as a pack.<br /> <br /> (Pure) Humans are excluded from the Packs.<br /> <br /> Kinfolks are able to join temporary if they know the Gift Tagalong or with the Bonding Rite (Level One, Glass Walker - Dies Ultimae; Glass Walkers Revised, pg. 82)<br /> <br /> The Ahadi &amp; Beast Courts have special &quot;Rite of Totem&quot; like Rites, which enables other Changers to join a packs. There are some &quot;specialities&quot;. For example an Ananasi wouldn't receive the Totem's benefits (and suffer some dis-Obligation) or a Nuwisha can just join into a pack of a Trickster Totem.<br /> <br /> Eastern Vampires &amp; Dhampyres are able to join the Mouuntain Shentais. They even have the a background Nushi, what is Totem with some addons.<br /> <br /> Nunnehi are able to ji\u00f3oin packs. Eshu also has a Background called Orisha, what works like Nunehi Totem with some modification. In their case the possibility of joining a pack is unclear.<br /> <br /> Mages Totem differs from the Fera's, but with enough medzsik anythingi is possible.<br /> <br /> Normaly nay to Mummies, Hunters, Demons, Vampires and Wraiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T13:56:50-08:00","id":1347549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347436#post1347436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eastern Vampires &amp; Dhampyres are able to join the Mouuntain Shentais. They even have the a background Nushi, what is Totem with some addons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not true. Sentai rites don't allow you to include nonFera. Totem Rite doesn't allow NonKJ. KJ have theirown rites for making Pack equivalents. THey cannot join True Pack equivalents though obviously any random group can join a wave sentai.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nunnehi are able to ji\u00f3oin packs. Eshu also has a Background called Orisha, what works like Nunehi Totem with some modification. In their case the possibility of joining a pack is unclear. </div> </div> </div>No, they may have Totems. Which is different from &quot;can join a pack&quot; Nunnehi and Eshu can't even pool together to make a Pack equivalent. THey can just have totems like how a Fera can have a personal Totem.<br /> <br /> If &quot;can have a totem&quot; counts then Pure Humans can join packs since they can have Totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages Totem differs from the Fera's, but with enough medzsik anythingi is possible. </div> </div> </div>By the rules there is no method for a Mage to join a Pack outside methods a Kinfolk might use if they are in fact kinfolk. There are plenty of things Magick cannot do contrary to popular belief(like say undo the curse of caine). This may be one of them. They may be able to simulate the effects with the help of a Totem but the half spirit connection is just not there so much like the KJ simulation may be all that is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T14:50:39-08:00","id":1347558,"title":"","content":"I don't see any reason why a Mage with the right Spheres (which would be rather high) and Focus couldn't facilitate a bond to become part of a Pack. It's not some super special power, it's not vastly violating any metaphysical rules of the setting, or anything like that. The thing is... it's fairly pointless for mages to do. A bunch of Dreamspeakers that form a &quot;pack&quot; with a shared Totem that works just like a Garou pack isn't really gaining much for the effort. Joining a mixed Garou and mages pack is.... nice for the pack but the social drawbacks are going to be immense and plot defining enough that it's only happening because the PCs are special cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T17:07:21-08:00","id":1347573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347558#post1347558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any reason why a Mage with the right Spheres (which would be rather high) and Focus couldn't facilitate a bond to become part of a Pack. It's not some super special power, it's not vastly violating any metaphysical rules of the setting, or anything like that. The thing is... it's fairly pointless for mages to do. A bunch of Dreamspeakers that form a &quot;pack&quot; with a shared Totem that works just like a Garou pack isn't really gaining much for the effort. Joining a mixed Garou and mages pack is.... nice for the pack but the social drawbacks are going to be immense and plot defining enough that it's only happening because the PCs are special cases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A group of mages with the right spheres could easily simulate many of the advantages of Pack and even gain some(mental communication, shared effects etc). As for whether or not Mages joining a Garou pack violates metaphysics, Packs are built upon unique qualities of Garou nature. Even the Rites that allow for multiple Fera types call upon their unique qualities. Mages are not Fera, even if with enough life they could &quot;Fake it&quot; same with spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T17:47:23-08:00","id":1347580,"title":"","content":"Do you need the Totem background to benefit from the Totem's individual / pack traits? Or it is enough that you are a werewolf member of the pack even without Totem points assigned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T23:48:18-08:00","id":1347623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347573#post1347573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A group of mages with the right spheres could easily simulate many of the advantages of Pack and even gain some(mental communication, shared effects etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>What, exactly, stops them from having all the benefits of a Pack? They can simulate all the advantages of a Pack with the right Spheres (and time) already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for whether or not Mages joining a Garou pack violates metaphysics, Packs are built upon unique qualities of Garou nature. Even the Rites that allow for multiple Fera types call upon their unique qualities. Mages are not Fera, even if with enough life they could &quot;Fake it&quot; same with spirit. </div> </div> </div>OK. What stops a mage with the right Spheres from creating a Spirit from nothing, who when acting as a Pack Totem allows the Pack to incorporate mages?<br /> <br /> I just find this a very strange line to draw... when mages can custom create spirits, the idea that they can't join a spiritual bond (even if it takes a new Fera rite instead of the traditional one or something) with Fera seems like it's not really putting anything in perspective. The Totem Rite also isn't built on unique qualities of the Garou. It's built on the established ancient spiritual relationships between spirits and Garou. It's the spirits that acknowledge the Rites and empower them, not the Garou. The Garou just enact them and the spirits are bound by their nature to honor Rites performed by Garou; they can actually choose to honor a Rite performed by anyone if they have a reason to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347580#post1347580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you need the Totem background to benefit from the Totem's individual / pack traits? Or it is enough that you are a werewolf member of the pack even without Totem points assigned?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need at least one Totem dot before you can get the full benefits of being in the Pack, however you can qualify for some perks without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T02:31:05-08:00","id":1347645,"title":"","content":"The Totem merit for humans is akint to a personal totem and I'd wager that this is prohibiting joining a pack with a pack totem, even if the Totem incarnae is the same.<br /> <br /> A mage could mimic the Tagalong gift with the right spheres, or even the bonding Rite of the Dies ultimae. Silver Novel has Albrecht &amp; Co run into a different pack with a deamspeaker. It isn't going into specifics about the rules, but it seemed like their mage companion was pretty much part of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:04:36-08:00","id":1347675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347623#post1347623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need at least one Totem dot before you can get the full benefits of being in the Pack, however you can qualify for some perks without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, what are those perks?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T08:06:24-08:00","id":1347685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347675#post1347675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, what are those perks?</div> </div> </div> </div>page 140 of W20 states: <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Until then, he\u2019s never really </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">part</span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of the pack in a way that the other members are: any </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Gifts or rites that affect the pack do not include the </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">character, and he cannot be a part of any pack tactics. </span></span>Until he has Pack Totem Background instead of Personal Totem, he\u2019s never really part of the pack in a way that the other members are: any Gifts or rites that affect the pack do not include the character, and he cannot be a part of any pack tactics. <br /> <br /> This is in regards to a character having Personal Totem and being with a pack... <br /> <br /> Revised and W20 both state Totem as a possible prerequisite for pack tactics, but possibly not the only way to achieve the pack maneuvers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Until then, he\u2019s never really </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">part</span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of the pack in a way that the other members are: any </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Gifts or rites that affect the pack do not include the </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">character, and he cannot be a part of any pack tactics. </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Until then, he\u2019s never really </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">part</span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of the pack in a way that the other members are: any </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Gifts or rites that affect the pack do not include the </span></span><span style=\"color:transparent\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">character, and he cannot be a part of any pack tactics. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T08:11:43-08:00","id":1347686,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> So if you are a werewolf without the Totem merit you still get access to Individual and Pack tratis provided by the Totem, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T11:09:42-08:00","id":1347718,"title":"","content":"The perks you can get:<br /> <br /> Pack Iniative<br /> Opening the Way<br /> Social benefits of being in a Pack instead of being considered Anruth (more important than it sounds, esp. regarding earning Renown).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T11:11:00-08:00","id":1347719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347686#post1347686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> So if you are a werewolf without the Totem merit you still get access to Individual and Pack tratis provided by the Totem, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say... depends.<br /> First, I believe even in W20 Totem is a background for werewolves. It is a merit for Kinfolk, possibly mages.<br /> So, despite gifts like the mentioned &quot;Tagalong&quot; you wouldn't get pack bonuses nor individual traits if you just happen to... well... tag along.<br /> <br /> But the process of forming a pack or joining a pack can be very different for each pack. Mari, Albrecht and Evan probably didn't perform a Rite to become a pack, it just happened as part of ... well, life. I don't believe they have a Totem, though. The signature pack from the novels also didn't formally form, their Totem even orchestrated that they would meet and form a pack out of circumstances. Other Packs are possibly more formal.<br /> <br /> But if there is an informal pack and one is with the pack all the time and kind of follows the ways of the Totem then at some point the joining of the pack is in progress and then traits should be available. Because, in theory, there is no rule that requires any member of the pack to give background points to the pack totem. I mean, if PCs are created as a pack an one player states &quot;I want all my freebies to go into Pure Breed and Mars Rising, and therefore can't contribute any points for pack totem&quot; then he isn't barred from being a pack member, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T11:20:07-08:00","id":1347720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347718#post1347718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pack Iniative</div> </div> </div> </div>Optional rule, but you are right, the totem is explicitly mentioned as requirement on page 267 of W20.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347718#post1347718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opening the Way</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this practice doesn't seem have this name anymore in W20. It states on page 309 that being in a pack is a requirement, but a totem is not. So, if totemless packs exist this might still be available to them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347718#post1347718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social benefits of being in a Pack instead of being considered Anruth (more important than it sounds, esp. regarding earning Renown).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ecxplixitly stated is a -3 Wisdom. One could handle that, possibly. But in general you are right, a pack is good for social life and renown...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:16:26-08:00","id":1347729,"title":"","content":"On top of that -3, there's also the rule that Packs share Renown for things they do together. When a Pack goes off, investigates a warehouse, finds a BSD and some fomori up to trouble, kill them all, and cleanse the place, and so on, the Renown goes to all members of the Pack as a single unit rather than worrying about who killed what, or who did which Rite.<br /> <br /> Not being a member of a Pack, even if assisting on such things, would mean having your Deeds analyzed separately (which might not always be bad, but is usually in play not a good thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T14:49:53-08:00","id":1347768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347623#post1347623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, exactly, stops them from having all the benefits of a Pack? They can simulate all the advantages of a Pack with the right Spheres (and time) already.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the right spheres(life and spirit) they can simulate all the advantages of being a were whatever but.. that doesn't make a Mage a Garou.<br /> <br /> They can build all the advantages from scratch<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OK. What stops a mage with the right Spheres from creating a Spirit from nothing, who when acting as a Pack Totem allows the Pack to incorporate mages? </div> </div> </div>That is some crazy amount of successes to make Incarna. I mean at this point I'd make the same argument that &quot;why can't I create my own High Umbral God to undo the curse of Caine&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just find this a very strange line to draw... when mages can custom create spirits, the idea that they can't join a spiritual bond (even if it takes a new Fera rite instead of the traditional one or something) with Fera seems like it's not really putting anything in perspective. </div> </div> </div>The Line I am drawing is Pack/Sentai. I never said &quot;Mages can't simulate this&quot; They can simulate alot of things. They could make theirown &quot;Pack&quot; rituals that gives various benefits to Fera and friends. That doesn't make it in all ways a Pack or Sentai.<br /> <br /> But yes, if you want to functionally build all the advantages of a Pack yourself a Mage can do it. Actually think of it this way Fera have access to a Car. A mage has to build hisown. Once he's built he can do the same things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Totem Rite also isn't built on unique qualities of the Garou. It's built on the established ancient spiritual relationships between spirits and Garou. It's the spirits that acknowledge the Rites and empower them, not the Garou. The Garou just enact them and the spirits are bound by their nature to honor Rites performed by Garou; they can actually choose to honor a Rite performed by anyone if they have a reason to. </div> </div> </div>Yes Rites are built on the established spiritual relationships Garou and other Fera have with Spirits. Mages do not have these relationships to fall back on. They may in fact have different equally valid and distinct relatiionships to fall back on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:58:29-08:00","id":1347797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347768#post1347768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the right spheres(life and spirit) they can simulate all the advantages of being a were whatever but.. that doesn't make a Mage a Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a strawman, because a mage doesn't need to be a Garou to have a spiritual bond with a Garou facilitated by a spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is some crazy amount of successes to make Incarna. </div> </div> </div>You don't need to create an Incarna. The Incarna aren't Pack Totems, the spirits that actually serve as Totems are lower ranking avatars of Incarna, and they don't have to all offer the same benefits. There's multiple versions of a few Totem spirits in the books.<br /> <br /> You don't need to invent a new Incarna, you can just custom make an Avatar of Uktena (or pick whichever mysticism orient Totem spirit) of a much lower rank..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Line I am drawing is Pack/Sentai. </div> </div> </div>The problem is this line doesn't make any sense from a WtA or MtA stand point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages do not have these relationships to fall back on. </div> </div> </div>They can, however, build them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T18:49:10-08:00","id":1347813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347797#post1347797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is a strawman, because a mage doesn't need to be a Garou to have a spiritual bond with a Garou facilitated by a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do. A Sentai is not a Pack. And whatever the Mage makes is neither of those things. They are constructing something new and different. No different than using Life to shapeshift into Crinos or using Spirit to enter the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need to create an Incarna. The Incarna aren't Pack Totems, the spirits that actually serve as Totems are lower ranking avatars of Incarna, and they don't have to all offer the same benefits. There's multiple versions of a few Totem spirits in the books.<br /> <br /> You don't need to invent a new Incarna, you can just custom make an Avatar of Uktena (or pick whichever mysticism orient Totem spirit) of a much lower rank.. </div> </div> </div>Which is generally approved of by said Incarna. SINCE we are apparently creating a whole new spirit from cloth now apparently we are hacking a Random Spirit without the Incarna's permission.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is this line doesn't make any sense from a WtA or MtA stand point. </div> </div> </div><br /> That's like saying using spheres to create a rock is the same as the gift create Element. Rites do particular things. That's why you can't use Rite of totem to say add a corax but you need a completely different rite that does that. The rite for forming a Sentai is a separate rite from Rite of Totem. They are not interchangeable.<br /> <br /> A Rite that allowed one to include a Mage would in turn be YET a different Rite. I am not saying its beyond a mage's power to develop... just it doesn't exist and would require development. There is not Rote for forming a pack. There is no Rote for joining a Pack. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can, however, build them. </div> </div> </div>They can build new and different connections. They cannot say build the thousands of years of connection a Tribe might have. They can call upon the thousands of years their Tradition might have developed with particular spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T00:07:02-08:00","id":1347841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347813#post1347813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what? Cite me something in the books that backs this up, esp. since you actually contradict this later in your own post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Sentai is not a Pack. And whatever the Mage makes is neither of those things. </div> </div> </div>The semantic game here is irrelevant to the actual end result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are constructing something new and different. </div> </div> </div>New yes, different not inherently. You've established no reason it has to be different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No different than using Life to shapeshift into Crinos or using Spirit to enter the Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Because you refuse to acknowledge that there are things mages can do that are actually the same as what a Garou does.<br /> <br /> A mage made Fetish and a Garou made Fetish work the same way and are interchangeable metaphysically. There aren't &quot;mage Fetishes&quot; and &quot;Garou Fetishes.&quot; There's just Fetishes despite who makes them and how.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is generally approved of by said Incarna. </div> </div> </div>This really isn't actually in the books. The avatar spirits are the only ones directly involved. It's assumed the Incarna approve because of the way spirits work; an avatar spirit can't naturally do something that wouldn't be something their Incarna approves of... though Wisdom and Cunning Incarnae are kinda flexible about stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...we are hacking a Random Spirit without the Incarna's permission. </div> </div> </div>No, we're creating a new member of the Incarna's brood. Something that happens naturally all the time. Rat doesn't take a direct interest every time a rodent infestation gets bad enough a few rat or mouse Gafflings are spawned in the local penumbra, but they're still Rat spirits that have the potential to grow to be powerful enough to be Pack Totems..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's like saying using spheres to create a rock is the same as the gift create Element. </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. It's saying that you're making up a line that the books don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are not interchangeable. </div> </div> </div>Great, I actually addressed this in two ways already: one a spirit that accepts individuals that aren't usually allowed by the Rite (something that can be done already), or a new Rite that still results in the same end result in terms of the actual results of creating a Pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is not Rote for forming a pack. There is no Rote for joining a Pack. </div> </div> </div>There's no official Rotes for lots of things that there's obviously Rotes for, as the Rote lists in the books are pretty short. Garou and mages have existed in the WoD for thousands of years, including kin-mages, so the idea that nobody's ever developed the Rote is a bit hard to believe. Finding it is a different matter (esp. since the groups most likely aren't the types to have libraries of grimoires around).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can build new and different connections. </div> </div> </div>Or they can jack into the existing connections. The connection of Garou and spirits isn't something that mages can't get involved with even if there are limits on what they could do with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T08:51:24-08:00","id":1347915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347719#post1347719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say... depends.<br /> First, I believe even in W20 Totem is a background for werewolves. It is a merit for Kinfolk, possibly mages.<br /> So, despite gifts like the mentioned &quot;Tagalong&quot; you wouldn't get pack bonuses nor individual traits if you just happen to... well... tag along.<br /> <br /> But the process of forming a pack or joining a pack can be very different for each pack. Mari, Albrecht and Evan probably didn't perform a Rite to become a pack, it just happened as part of ... well, life. I don't believe they have a Totem, though. The signature pack from the novels also didn't formally form, their Totem even orchestrated that they would meet and form a pack out of circumstances. Other Packs are possibly more formal.<br /> <br /> But if there is an informal pack and one is with the pack all the time and kind of follows the ways of the Totem then at some point the joining of the pack is in progress and then traits should be available. Because, in theory, there is no rule that requires any member of the pack to give background points to the pack totem. I mean, if PCs are created as a pack an one player states &quot;I want all my freebies to go into Pure Breed and Mars Rising, and therefore can't contribute any points for pack totem&quot; then he isn't barred from being a pack member, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But my point is, Jack, Jill and Bill are playing; Bill and Jill spend ALL of their background dots into getting Totem (Polar Bear) with a 10 point cost.<br /> <br /> Jack puts all his Background dots into Pure Breed and Resources... Does he is still gets the Individual / Pack benefits that the totem provides even if he did not put a single dot into the Totem background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-12-2019, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:41:34-08:00","id":1347977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347915#post1347915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he is still gets the Individual / Pack benefits that the totem provides even if he did not put a single dot into the Totem background?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he only gets the things I posted earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:55:48-08:00","id":1348229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1347977#post1347977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, he only gets the things I posted earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just re-read the W20 section of Totem and i have to disagree. If the PCs are created as a pack and all PCs are members of the pack, per start of the game, and Jack is roleplaying his character as part of the pack and follower of &quot;Polar Bear&quot;, then there is nothing in the rules prohibiting him from gaining the bonuses the totem grants.<br /> <br /> I mean, players might create their characters trying to cover all their bases in what a pack would need. So, if all three are okay with the fact that Jack spends his dots on Pure Breed and Resources while they are not, then that is okay.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> It states, the Totem is bought for the Pack when the Background cost is met. If Polar Bear was to cost 10 Points and it grants its power to the entire pack then math dictates that 5 + 5 + 0 = 5 + 4 + 1 (or any other combination that sums to 10).<br /> <br /> EDIT 2:<br /> That is under the premise that there is consensus (in- and out-of-character) that they are and act as a Pack. It would be a different circumstance if one were to roleplay the formation of a pack or the joining into an existing pack. Even in that case there is no rule requiring to invest experience into Totem background, but I'd rule that the consensus must be reached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 11-13-2019, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T09:40:52-08:00","id":1348279,"title":"","content":"The Totem Rite says that characters must have dots in the Totem Background to benefit from the Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T03:33:31-08:00","id":1348449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1348279#post1348279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Totem Rite says that characters must have dots in the Totem Background to benefit from the Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate W20 for not having relevant information cross-referenced, however...<br /> <br /> You are right, it states:<br /> <i>&quot;Characters must purchase the Totem Background to benefit from this rite. Otherwise, the rite is simply not performed.&quot;</i><br /> That imho means, that the characters (as a group) need to have had purchased the Totem Background, or the Rite will not be performed.<br /> The Totem Background clearly states:<br /> <i>&quot;Totem is a Background that applies directly to the character\u2019s pack, rather than the individual.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Therefore, the entry at the &quot;Rite of the Totem&quot; shouldn't be read as &quot;each individual needs to have at least one dot&quot;, for individuals should never have a dot in Totem, only the pack has dots as a group (Personal Totems notwithstanding). And even individuals who didn't contribute are members of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T11:40:44-08:00","id":1348531,"title":"","content":"Or, you know, it's one of the many things that got copy &amp; pasted from Revised and they forgot to include the Revised ST Handbook FAQ when doing so.<br /> <br /> Given the state of things, I'm not incline to get into a parsing war on this. The Revised FAQ is more than enough insight into the intent of the game to pick how to interpret the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T04:29:22-08:00","id":1348639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1346711-pack-membership?p=1348531#post1348531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, it's one of the many things that got copy &amp; pasted from Revised and they forgot to include the Revised ST Handbook FAQ when doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... so many things.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}